{"attempt":2,"candidate":{"formalization":{"error":"The required executable contract cannot faithfully represent the specified output and implementation restrictions in the supplied registered frontend. The Lean source declares the actual input fields and establishes a concrete satisfiability witness; it does not assert that the remaining obligations are discharged.","gaps":[{"description":"The required return value is JSON null for any directed cycle, otherwise a list of two-element integer lists. The supplied AST sorts provide no nullable-list sort or documented serialization mapping that makes Unit or Except produce this exact null-or-list output. Substituting an error constructor, output record, or empty list for null changes the specification.","obligations":["O1","O3","O5","E1"]},{"description":"The registered mathematical term and formula language cannot establish restrictions on Python dependencies, external I/O, file reads, network use, printing, or retained state.","obligations":["S1"]}],"preserved_obligations":["D1","A1","O1","O2","O3","O4","O5","S1","E1"],"preserved_requirements":{"assumption":"Caller inputs conform to the graph specification. The empty graph provides a satisfiability witness.","examples":"The n=3 graph with edges [[0,1],[1,2],[0,2],[0,2]] returns [[0,1],[1,2]]. The n=1 graph with edges [[0,0]] returns null.","implementation":"solution.py exposes pure deterministic Python 3 solve(data), returns JSON-serializable values, uses only the standard library, performs no external I/O, and retains no state across calls.","input":"solve receives one JSON object with integer n from 0 through 10 and edges containing directed pairs [u,v].","output":"Ignore duplicate directed edges. Return JSON null whenever any directed cycle exists anywhere, including self-loops and disconnected components. For acyclic inputs return precisely the unique original edges having no alternate path of at least two edges, as two-element lists sorted lexicographically by source then destination. Preserve every directed reachability relation, include no redundant edges, and represent isolated vertices implicitly. Edgeless graphs including n=0 return an empty list."},"required_extension":"A registered executable nullable-list sort with explicit null-or-list JSON serialization and branch semantics, together with implementation checks for the S1 restrictions. Opaque Lean acceptance cannot substitute for the requested strict Python TESTED assurance.","status":"unsupported_domain"},"lean_source":"namespace VeriSlop\nstructure Input where\n  n : Int\n  edges : List (List Int)\n\ndef conforms (input : Input) : Prop :=\n  0 ≤ input.n ∧ input.n ≤ 10 ∧\n  ∀ edge ∈ input.edges, ∃ u v : Int,\n    edge = [u, v] ∧ 0 ≤ u ∧ u < input.n ∧ 0 ≤ v ∧ v < input.n\n\ntheorem conforms_empty : conforms ⟨0, []⟩ := by\n  simp [conforms]\nend VeriSlop\n"},"critique":{"attempt":2,"diagnostics":[],"encoding":"verislop.autonomous-critique/0.1","feedback":["CRITIC DIAGNOSTIC REPAIR: Replace the unsupported-domain report with a schema-conforming formalization artifact containing the required schema_version, artifact_kind, profile_id, lean_toolchain, lean_file, bindings, and internal_obligations fields. Use actual registered values rather than inventing a profile or serialization mapping; preserve all required obligations.","CRITIC DIAGNOSTIC REPAIR: Remove the unexpected top-level status property and the other rejected report properties identified by diagnostics 9 through 13. Report unsupported-domain limitations through an accepted diagnostic mechanism rather than substituting this report for the required formalization artifact.","CRITIC DIAGNOSTIC REPAIR: The provided Lean source establishes only input conformance for the empty graph. Resolving this blocking diagnostic requires a supported executable contract for the exact null-or-list output and checks for the implementation restrictions; the satisfiability witness alone does not discharge those guarantees."],"mile